both of them alpha. And we'll say that the&nbsp;
point where these two intersect is P. 
&nbsp;

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:45.280
And now like, a lot of Euclid-style proofs,&nbsp;
we're just going to draw some new lines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:50.240
figure out what things must be equal, and get some&nbsp;
conclusions. For instance, let's draw the line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:56.000
from P which is perpendicular to the side length&nbsp;
