my drawing is a little bit sloppy, but the logic&nbsp;
helps us see that they do have to be the same. 
&nbsp;

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:41.120
Next I'll draw a line from P down to B, and then&nbsp;
from P down to C, and I claim that this triangle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:46.880
here is congruent to its reflection across that&nbsp;
perpendicular bisector, which will be CPD. Again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:51.120
the symmetry maybe helps make this clear, but&nbsp;
more rigorously they both have the same base,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:55.280
they both have a 90 degree angle, and they&nbsp;
both have the same height, so it follows by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.280 --> 00:08:00.000
the side-angle-side relation. So based on that&nbsp;
first pair of triangles, I'm going to mark this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.160
side length here as being the same as this side&nbsp;
length here, marking them with double tick marks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.120
And based on the second triangle&nbsp;
relation I'll mark this side length here&nbsp;&nbsp;

